  { q: "Is a VPS better than TCPShield's or Infinity-Filter's free plan?", a: "Usually not in raw protection. Those services filter Minecraft traffic specifically and spread attacks over a larger network. A VPS wins on control, privacy and limits: no third party in the connection, no player or bandwidth cap from a protection plan, and everything configurable." },
  { q: "Does Hetzner or OVH protect a Minecraft server on a VPS?", a: "Both filter attacks on the network level for free. Hetzner names reflection attacks, UDP floods and SYN floods. OVHcloud's game-specific filtering is tied to its dedicated game servers; its VPS range gets the general protection. Neither promises to understand the Minecraft protocol on a VPS." },
